        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 89-year-old female patient, admitted on 26th November 2017 due to an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed the exacerbation. Blood tests were obtained to exclude infectious or other systemic causes. She was promptly treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy. Vital signs were monitored closely throughout her stay. She responded well to treatment with improvement in respiratory function and oxygenation. Patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management was provided prior to discharge. We recommend close follow-up and optimisation of her maintenance inhaler regimen. Please do not hesitate to contact us should you have any questions.</div>"
            },
